## Ask a coach

Tap **Ask to be coached** on a coach's profile, or open the link they shared. You answer a few
questions (what you want, how long you've trained, any injuries…) and pick the package you're
interested in. Only the coach sees your answers, and nothing else is shared.

Your request is a conversation with the coach: in **Messages › Requests › Sent** on the phone, or
**My coach** on the web. They might ask you something first, then:

- **Offer you a spot.** The offer shows as a card with the package, the price and how long they're
  holding the spot. Take it before then, or ask them to offer it again if it runs out.
- **Put you on their waiting list** when they're full. They offer you a spot when one opens; you
  can leave the list any time.
- **Say it's not a fit.** Nothing was shared or paid. Delete the request and your answers go.

## Take the spot

**Take the spot** opens a page on the web with the package, when you start and when you're first
charged, what the coach will see (change it any time), and the coach's agreement if they wrote one:
read it and tick that you agree. Paying needs you to be 18 or over; under 18, ask the coach to sort
payment outside LogIt. You pay the coach on Stripe's page, then you're straight back, coached. If you
already have a coach, taking a spot ends that coaching: a plan through LogIt stops renewing, and you
keep that coach until the end of what you paid for.

You can change your answers or withdraw while the request is open. If you don't have the app yet,
you get an email when the coach replies (stop them from the link in the email).

If a coach invited you by username, accept it in My coach. Some coaches charge through their link:
you pay on the link's page before coaching starts.

<HowTo id="pro.coach" />

## Stopping

**Stop coaching** on My coach. With a monthly plan it stops renewing, and coaching carries on until
the end of what you paid for; otherwise it ends straight away. Your program, meal plan and history
stay yours. If your card fails, **Update card** opens Stripe's page and the payment is tried again as
soon as you're back. If your coach hasn't replied for a week, you can stop with the unused days
refunded. Blocking your coach also ends coaching, with the unused days refunded.

## Check-ins

When your coach gives you a check-in form, it shows as Due under Check-ins on the phone, or My coach on
the web. After they review it you'll see their reply with it.

